From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taynotfound <marztayron@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rain-0985: GPU pool 0x90000000-0xC0000000

First gpu=1 boot panicked: "IOMemoryDescriptor physical with managed page
0x90000000:0x4000000", then pmap_enter_pv: unexpected PV head. topaz's
GPU pool (1 GB at 0x90000000) is unmanaged there; on rain the --midmem
ADT gave the kernel 0x80000000 + 3 GiB. Kernel RAM moves to the 0xC0000000
bank (2 GiB) and the pool shrinks to 768 MB, ending where that bank starts.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp
index 16da336..2c794f1 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,12 @@ kbuf_pa(struct kbuf *b, uint64_t off)
  * the GPU's, mapped write-combined (Normal non-cacheable: no cache upkeep).
  */
 #define GPU_POOL_BASE       0x90000000ull
-#define GPU_POOL_SIZE       0x40000000ull       /* 1 GB */
+/*
+ * rain: 768 MB, 0x90000000-0xC0000000, the rest of the 0x80000000 bank. The kernel's RAM is the
+ * 0xC0000000 bank (mkadt.py --midmem with MIDBASE=0xc0000000 MIDSIZE=0x80000000); topaz's 1 GB
+ * ran into it (pmap_enter_pv: unexpected PV head on a managed page).
+ */
+#define GPU_POOL_SIZE       0x30000000ull
 #define GPU_POOL_UNIT       0x10000ull          /* 64 KB */
 #define GPU_POOL_CHUNK      0x4000000ull        /* 64 MB: mapped on first use (1 GB at once is more IO space than there is) */
 #define GPU_POOL_CHUNKS     (GPU_POOL_SIZE / GPU_POOL_CHUNK)
